  <section>
    <h2>The problem: the index is the expensive part</h2>
    <p>
      In multimodal retrieval, the index built from a deployed embedding model is often the
      largest asset in the serving stack — re-embedding a billion-document corpus can take
      weeks of GPU time. Adapting that model to a new domain therefore carries a second cost
      beyond fine-tuning: index migration. Current methods force a trade-off.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="results">
